From 58dac3138ad2c07e4236514f6e3700368796a2a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:21:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm: ATSAME51J20A SoC and the curiosity-circuitpython
 board

The SAM E51 through the generic SoC, built from the generated
ATSAME51J20A descriptor: a Cortex-M4F (CPUID r0p1), instances with
several consecutive NVIC lines (mchp-regblock gains per-line IRQ outputs
and an irq_lines hook), backup RAM, and the SAM D5x models: OSCCTRL
U2401 (XOSC0/1, DFLL48M, FDPLL0/1), OSC32KCTRL U2400, MCLK U2408,
NVMCTRL U2409, TRNG U2242, QSPI U2008 (serial memory mode on an SSI bus,
memory window at 0x04000000) and the USB U2222 device controller with a
built-in host that enumerates the device and bridges its CDC ACM
interface to a chardev. GCLK numbers GENCTRL.SRC per family. New
SST26VF016B/032B/064B quad SPI flash. Regenerated tables for all four
devices.

The Curiosity CircuitPython board (EV78P89A, the PyKit Explorer's
controller): 32.768 kHz crystal, SST26VF032B on QSPI (-drive if=mtd),
LED D13 (PB23), USER (PA27), USB console, debug and BLE UARTs, the UF2
bootloader's start of an image at 0x4000. Stock CircuitPython 10.1.4
boots to its REPL. qtest curiosity-cp-test.

Peripheral Pretender: AI-assisted, not for upstream QEMU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
